WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.635
To plan a meeting, you need to know when people are free.

00:00:04.635 --> 00:00:09.135
This video shows how to look at one person's schedule or everyone's, how

00:00:09.135 --> 00:00:13.578
busy and free time are decided, how the Team Availability page lays out

00:00:13.578 --> 00:00:17.270
a team's day, and how to find a time that everyone shares.

00:00:21.873 --> 00:00:26.379
Under the calendar list, Whose schedule shows the events of other people.

00:00:26.379 --> 00:00:28.603
Choose Everyone, and choose Show.

00:00:28.603 --> 00:00:34.649
The calendar now shows the events on everyone's own calendars, and the events they attend, together.

00:00:34.649 --> 00:00:38.642
This helps a manager see a team's workload, or check a busy week

00:00:38.642 --> 00:00:40.353
before moving a meeting.

00:00:40.804 --> 00:00:47.067
To follow one person, choose Choose people, search for a name, pick Jamie, and choose Show.

00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:52.684
The calendar shows his own calendars and the events he attends, and nothing else.

00:00:56.753 --> 00:01:01.679
Events you are not allowed to open show as Busy, with their time and no title.

00:01:01.679 --> 00:01:06.957
Whose schedule only appears for people with the permission to list anyone's calendar

00:01:06.957 --> 00:01:12.353
events, and opening the details needs the permission to view anyone's calendar events.

00:01:16.553 --> 00:01:20.892
Whether someone is free is worked out from all of their calendars, and

00:01:20.892 --> 00:01:23.919
from the events they attend on other calendars.

00:01:23.919 --> 00:01:27.973
An event that is confirmed and shown as Busy makes the time busy.

00:01:28.723 --> 00:01:31.502
A tentative event shows as tentative.

00:01:31.502 --> 00:01:35.961
An event shown as Free, and kinds of events that leave the time

00:01:35.961 --> 00:01:41.195
free, such as a holiday, a reminder or a milestone, don't make anyone busy.

00:01:41.195 --> 00:01:43.263
A cancelled event is gone.

00:01:47.463 --> 00:01:51.963
With Team Calendars on, open Calendars, then Team Availability.

00:01:51.963 --> 00:01:58.093
Choose the team's calendar, the Day, and the Meeting length in minutes, and choose Show.

00:01:58.544 --> 00:02:02.949
Every member of the team gets a row, with a cell for each half hour.

00:02:02.949 --> 00:02:07.354
Red is busy, yellow is tentative, and green is free, worked out from

00:02:07.354 --> 00:02:09.557
all of that person's calendars.

00:02:09.557 --> 00:02:14.259
Here the quarterly planning makes all three busy at one in the afternoon,

00:02:14.259 --> 00:02:18.604
and Sam's dentist appointment, which is tentative, shows in yellow.

00:02:19.056 --> 00:02:23.248
Under the grid, When everyone is free lists the gaps long enough for

00:02:23.248 --> 00:02:25.854
the meeting that all of the team shares.

00:02:25.854 --> 00:02:30.046
Ask for a longer meeting, and the shorter gaps drop out of the list.

00:02:30.496 --> 00:02:33.142
Pick another day and choose Show again.

00:02:33.142 --> 00:02:37.022
With more than one team calendar, you choose the team first.

00:02:37.022 --> 00:02:41.079
Once you have found a gap, add the event to the team's calendar

00:02:41.079 --> 00:02:42.725
and invite the people.

00:02:42.725 --> 00:02:46.429
The page shows the times in the time zone of the site, so

00:02:46.429 --> 00:02:48.546
everyone reads the same hours.

00:02:50.546 --> 00:02:54.906
Look at one schedule or everyone's, read the busy and free time, and

00:02:54.906 --> 00:02:58.854
let Team Availability list the gaps that suit the whole team.

00:02:58.854 --> 00:03:00.386
Thanks for watching.

